																		Some questions, comments and nitpicks =o)
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lexagon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1411139); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1411139&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609254834" alt="Lexagon" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1411139)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lexagon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1411139); return false;" >Lexagon</a></span> <span class="odate time_1348720373 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Sep 2012 04:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1574729">
									

<blockquote>
<p>500 square meter area of exclusion</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not sure what this means. Might be better to describe the exclusion zone in terms of distance from the edge of the football field &quot;50 meter wide zone surrounding the active area&quot; or something.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a 5 meter tall and 1.5 meter thick concrete fence</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That sounds more like something you'd call a wall rather than a fence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>all site personnel are to monitor the length and intensity of the sound produced by SCP-332 from soundproofed observation areas</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If they're soundproofed, how can they monitor the sound from within them?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>30 humanoids</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Assuming that we can see them, can you give more detail than just &quot;humanoids&quot;? Are they animated corpses? Planet-of-the-Apes monkey-creatures? Lizardmen?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-332 will also emit sound</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What kind of sound? Do they play their instruments? Screech like the pod people in Invasion of the Body Snatchers? Hoot like gorillas?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>if a noise between 15 and 80,000&#160;Hz is made</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's a huge range, human hearing tops out around I think 15-20k-ish.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The camera is picked up and pans around the room. Several deceased persons are visible in frame, including the original cameraman</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What did they die of? They're still in the room, I'm assuming they didn't get trampled?</p>
<p>I'm not voting atm, it feels like it still needs work to me. I must say that the unidentified person picking up the camera and panning around after everyone in the room is dead freaks me out, in a good way. I'm also pretty sure we've never had an anomolous marching band before, so that's a plus.</p>

							</div>

								
